Done. `dispatch` now retries each job up to `maxAttempts` (default 3), sleeping `baseDelayMs * 2 ** (attempt - 1)` between attempts (default 100ms, real timer), validates both options with `RangeError` before touching the queue, tags every processed/failed entry with 1-based `attempts`, and logs exactly one line per job at its final outcome. Added tests for retry-then-succeed, exhaustion with last error, exponential backoff across jobs, and invalid options leaving the queue intact — all 32 tests pass.
